<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
		Hardened-runtime entitlements for Teletype (F-08).

		Wired via bundle.macOS.entitlements in tauri.conf.json. tauri-cli
		2.12 signs with hardened runtime enabled by default, so this file
		must exist before the first signed build: a hardened-runtime app
		without the matching entitlements cannot record audio or read
		Contacts.

		Each key and why it is needed:

		com.apple.security.device.audio-input
			The app's entire purpose is dictation: it captures the
			microphone (cpal, 16 kHz mono). Under hardened runtime the
			NSMicrophoneUsageDescription string in Info.plist is not
			enough; the entitlement is also required.

		com.apple.security.personal-information.addressbook
			The app reads and writes the system address book
			(personalization, contact names in dictated text).
			NSContactsUsageDescription in Info.plist alone is not enough
			under hardened runtime; the entitlement is required.

		com.apple.security.automation.apple-events
			The app sends Apple Events to other applications to place
			dictated text where the user was typing (key simulation
			fallback). Without this, hardened runtime blocks the
			events outright.

		NOT included, and why:

		com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit
			Not needed: the app does not execute JIT-compiled code.
			The webview (WKWebView) runs in its own process, which is
			Apple's own code and is exempt. llama-server is a separate
			process with its own entitlements (none required: it is a
			plain CPU/Metal inference server, no JIT).

		com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation
			Not needed: every dylib the app loads is linked in at
			build time and lives inside the app bundle (the Swift
			FluidAudio static library is linked into the binary, not
			loaded at runtime). No unsigned or user-provided dylibs
			are loaded.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.personal-information.addressbook</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
